1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,370
Listen. Practice. Speak. Practice makes you perfect.

2
00:00:12,370 --> 00:00:21,360
Good morning. Thank you for meeting with us today. We appreciate the opportunity to discuss this proposal in detail.

3
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:31,360
Good morning. Thank you for hosting us. We are interested in moving forward, but there are several areas we'd like to negotiate before making a final decision.

4
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:34,480
That's completely understandable.

5
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:37,200
Please feel free to raise any concerns.

6
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,640
Our objective is to reach a solution that works well for both sides.

7
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:44,760
To begin with, I'd like to address pricing.

8
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:49,520
After reviewing your proposal, we notice that your unit price is higher than what we are

9
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:52,560
currently paying our existing supplier.

10
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:54,040
I see.

11
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:56,360
Price is always a critical factor.

12
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:03,360
However, our pricing reflects product consistency, quality standards, and supply reliability, which

13
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,200
we believe add long-term value.

14
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:12,540
We acknowledge the quality aspect, but internally the comparison is largely based on numbers.

15
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:16,640
At the moment, the difference is approximately 12%.

16
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,640
Thank you for being direct.

17
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:24,240
That gap is significant, but it may be possible to reduce it depending on volume commitments

18
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,560
and contracts duration.

19
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:31,960
We're open to discussing volume, but we need clarity on what kind of commitment would justify

20
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,640
a price revision.

21
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:39,280
Currently, the quotation is based on a monthly volume of 7,000 units.

22
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:44,640
If you can increase that to 10,000 units, we could offer a better rate.

23
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:49,620
Increasing volume is possible, but only if the pricing becomes more competitive.

24
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:52,380
What kind of reduction are we talking about?

25
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:59,060
With a volume of 10,000 units per month, we could reduce the price by around 6%.

26
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:02,420
That's an improvement, but it still doesn't meet our expectations.

27
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:08,180
Ideally, we're looking at a minimum 10% reduction to justify the switch.

28
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:12,380
A 10% reduction is challenging under the current terms.

29
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:18,260
However, if we consider a longer term agreement, there may be room for further adjustment.

30
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:21,080
How long a contract are you suggesting?

31
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:26,360
If we move from a six-month agreement to a 12-month contract, we can achieve better

32
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:29,640
production planning and cost efficiencies.

33
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:34,800
A one-year contract could be acceptable, provided there are clear performance benchmarks

34
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,320
and review points.

35
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:38,160
That's reasonable.

36
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:43,060
We can include quarterly performance reviews and service level evaluations.

37
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:47,640
In that case, what discount could you offer with a one-year commitment and increased

38
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,000
volume?

39
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,220
Under those conditions, we could improve the discount to around eight and a half percent.

40
00:02:54,220 --> 00:02:57,820
I appreciate the flexibility, but I need to be honest.

41
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:02,340
Without reaching 10%, internal approval will be very difficult.

42
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:04,660
I understand your position.

43
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:10,300
If we meet the 10% target, we would need some risk-sharing mechanisms in place.

44
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:13,540
What kind of risk-sharing are you referring to?

45
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:16,180
Primarily, demand forecasting.

46
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:21,920
If you can provide rolling forecasts, even indicative ones, it would help us manage inventory

47
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,300
and raw material costs.

48
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:29,980
We can provide forecasts, but accuracy beyond one month can't be guaranteed due to market

49
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:31,820
fluctuations.

50
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,380
That's acceptable.

51
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:37,660
Even non-binding forecasts would be beneficial for planning purposes.

52
00:03:37,660 --> 00:03:42,220
Alright, another area we need to discuss is payment terms.

53
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,740
Our standard policy is 60 days credit.

54
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:48,820
Our usual terms are 45 days.

55
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:53,100
Extending to 60 days increases our financing costs.

56
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:59,300
I understand, but adjusting payment terms internally is extremely complex for us.

57
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:05,060
If we agreed to 60 days, would you consider an advance payment for the initial period?

58
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:09,220
Possibly, but it would need to be reasonable and time-bound.

59
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:14,700
We could propose a 20% advance for the first two months, after which the 60-day

60
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:21,660
credit would apply fully. That seems manageable. I'll need internal confirmation, but in principle,

61
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:27,980
it could work. That's good to hear. Let's also talk about delivery and service levels,

62
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:35,500
as reliability is a key part of our offering. Yes, reliability is very important to us. We've faced

63
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:42,380
supply disruptions in the past, and we want to avoid that. We can commit to a 98% on time

64
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:49,180
delivery rate. And if that level isn't met? We can include a service penalty clause, such as

65
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:55,420
issuing credit notes for delays beyond an agreed threshold. That would give us more confidence.

66
00:04:55,420 --> 00:05:01,980
At the same time, demand can be unpredictable on our side. We understand. We can allow a

67
00:05:01,980 --> 00:05:09,500
plus or minus 15% flexibility on monthly forecasts without penalties. That flexibility is helpful.

68
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:15,500
Based on everything discussed so far, can you now confirm whether the 10% discount is achievable?

69
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:22,500
Considering the increased volume, one-year contract, forecast sharing, advanced payment,

70
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:27,500
and agreed service terms, yes, we can agree to a 10% unit discount.

71
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:32,500
That's excellent. This makes the proposal much more viable for us.

72
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:37,500
I'm glad we could align. Shall we recap to ensure everything is clear?

73
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,400
Yes, please.

74
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:46,520
We're agreeing on a one-year contract, a minimum monthly volume of 10,000 units, a 10% unit

75
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:53,680
price discount, 60-day credit terms after an initial 20% advance for two months, forecast

76
00:05:53,680 --> 00:06:01,000
sharing with a 15% flexibility range, and a 98% on-time delivery commitment with service

77
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,480
penalties.

78
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:06,080
That summary is accurate and reflects our discussion well.

79
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,080
Great.

80
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:12,680
We'll prepare a revised proposal and draft agreement incorporating all these points.

81
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:18,240
Please share those documents as soon as possible so we can proceed with internal approvals.

82
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,840
We'll send everything by tomorrow morning.

83
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,840
Perfect.

84
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:25,720
Once approved, we should be able to move forward without delay.

85
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:30,680
We're confident this partnership will be successful and mutually beneficial.

86
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:32,040
We feel the same.

87
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:35,800
Thank you for a professional and constructive negotiation.

88
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,800
Thank you as well.

89
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:40,900
We look forward to working together.

90
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:41,900
Good morning.

91
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:44,460
I appreciate you making time for this meeting.

92
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:49,940
I believe we're at a critical stage where we can address the remaining concerns and work

93
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:52,500
toward finalizing the agreement.

94
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:53,500
Good morning.

95
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,500
Thank you.

96
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:59,360
Yes, we've reviewed your proposal and overall see value, but there are still several

97
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:03,100
