102
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:21,100
While the quality and service you offer are strong, the overall cost is still higher

103
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:24,460
than what our finance team is comfortable approving.

104
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:25,900
I understand.

105
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:31,940
Our pricing reflects not only the product but also reliability, service, and long-term

106
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:36,540
operational efficiency, which often reduces hidden costs.

107
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:40,940
That said, we can explore options to make the numbers more competitive.

108
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:42,620
We appreciate that.

109
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:48,660
Internally, the target is roughly an 8 to 10% reduction on first-year costs.

110
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:53,140
We can work toward that by combining a moderate upfront discount

111
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:58,060
with incentives tied to volume commitments or multi-year contracts.

112
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:01,700
Can you provide more detail on how those incentives would work?

113
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:02,700
Certainly.

114
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:07,940
For instance, we could offer a base discount of 6% immediately.

115
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:14,380
If the monthly order volume exceeds a specified target, an additional 2-3% reduction would

116
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:15,700
be applied.

117
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:19,920
The challenge is that the first year volume is uncertain.

118
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:24,820
Would it be possible to phase the discount based on actual achieved volumes?

119
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:25,820
Absolutely.

120
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:28,380
We can structure the discount in tiers.

121
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:34,700
The first level applies to the base volume with incremental reductions as volumes increase

122
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,460
