123
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:40,420
That approach seems workable and easier to justify internally.

124
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:44,300
Another lever we can use is contract duration.

125
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:49,620
Longer agreements justify stronger discounts and better cost predictability.

126
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:52,580
Currently we're looking at a one-year contract.

127
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:54,260
How long would you propose?

128
00:08:54,260 --> 00:09:00,000
A two- or three-year framework agreement would allow us to offer more favorable terms while

129
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,700
maintaining operational stability.

130
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:08,040
Two years is feasible, provided there are clear exit clauses for underperformance or market

131
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,540
