171
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:11,720
How do you propose we mitigate these risks?

172
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:17,400
Through clear contingency plans, outlining responsibilities, communication protocols,

173
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,880
and decision-making authority.

174
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:24,320
Annual reviews would update the plan based on evolving conditions.

175
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:28,080
That level of preparation would satisfy our leadership team.

176
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,280
Another topic is communication.

177
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:34,160
Misalignment often arises from poor information flow.

178
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,160
Agreed.

179
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:38,560
How frequently do you suggest formal communications?

180
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:45,920
Monthly operational calls, quarterly management reviews, and ad hoc escalation for urgent matters.

181
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,360
That works for us.

182
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:53,080
Finally, we want to ensure transparency in all agreements, from pricing to operational

183
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:56,080
