184
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:57,360
Absolutely.

185
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:01,080
Teared documentation is key for internal approvals.

186
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:07,220
Based on today's discussion, we can summarize tiered pricing with volume incentives, staged

187
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:13,500
payment terms transitioning from 60 to 90 days, buffer stock support, service level

188
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:20,840
agreements with credits, joint quality audits, KPIs with regular review cycles, and collaborative

189
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,900
improvement initiatives.

190
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:25,440
That accurately captures our discussion.

191
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:26,440
Excellent.

192
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:31,440
Next step is to prepare a revised contract reflecting all these points.

193
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:36,440
Once we receive it, we'll review internally and aim to finalize within two weeks.

194
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:38,440
That timeline works for us.

195
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:41,440
Thank you for your constructive and transparent approach.

196
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:47,440
Thank you as well. We're confident this partnership will be long-term and mutually beneficial.

197
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:55,540
Agreed. We look forward to reviewing the draft and moving forward.

198
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:58,540
Good morning. Thank you for meeting with us again.

199
00:13:58,540 --> 00:14:02,180
I believe this is an important stage in our discussions.

200
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:03,180
Good morning.

201
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:04,860
Yes, I agree.

202
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:10,260
We've made good progress so far, and today we'd like to see if we can align on the remaining

203
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:11,260
